<title>UK: LME copper ends AM barely firmer, unsettled.</title>
<headline>LME copper ends AM barely firmer, unsettled.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Three months ends AM kerb touch stronger at $2,370.</p>
<p>Cash/threes slightly narrower at $70/75 backwardation.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Firmer, edging towards $1,642 resistance.</p>
<p>ZINC - Slightly stronger. LEAD - Little changed.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Slips to $7,400. TIN - Breaks below $5,700.</p>
<p>ALLOY - Quiet, little changed.</p>
</text>
